<name><surname>Leshabari</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Mpangile</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaaya</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kihwele</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>From teenage unwanted pregnancy to induced abortion: who facilitates links?</article-title><source>Int J Adolesc Youth</source><year>1994</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>195</fpage><lpage>210</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12290193</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mpangile</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Leshabari</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Kihwele</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors associated with induced abortion in public hospitals in Dar es Salaam</article-title><source>Reprod Health Matters</source><year>1993</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0968-8080(93)90004-D</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ngalinda</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><source>Age at first birth, fertility and contraception in Tanzania</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>PhD Thesis, University of Humboldt, Faculty of Philosophy, Berlin:</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weinstein</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ngallaba</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cross</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Mburu</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><source>Tanzania knowledge, attitudes and practices survey:Demographic and Health S