tention to be sexually active among Tanzanian school children</article-title><source>East Afr Med J</source><year>1996</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>218</fpage><lpage>224</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8706602</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anochie</surname><given-names>IC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ikpeme</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevalence of sexual activity and outcome among female secondary school students in Port Harcourt, Nigeria</article-title><source>Afr J Reprod Health</source><year>2001</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12471914</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/3583431</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ehlers</surname><given-names>VJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Maja</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sellers</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Gololo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adolescent mothers' utilization of reproductive health services in the Gauteng Province of the Republic of South Africa</article-title><source>Curationis</source><year>2000</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11949156</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ojengbede</surname><given-names>OA</given-names></name><name><surname>Otolorin</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name><name><surname>Fabanwo</surname><given-names>AO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pregnancy performance of Nigerian women aged 16 years and below, as seen in Ibadan, Nigeria</article-title><source>Afr J Med Med Sci</source><year>1987</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2821782</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blake</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><collab>Middlestadt.</collab></person-group><source>School-based programs to prevent HIV/AIDS: An overview of strategies used and lessons learned</source><series>11th International Conference on AIDS, Vancouver, July 7th-12th 1999</series><year>1999</year><publisher-name>International AIDS Society</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kowalewski</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jahn</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimatta</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Why do at risk mothers fail to reach referral level care? Barriers beyond distance and cost</article-title><source>Afr J Reprod Health</source><year>2000</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>100</fpage><lpage>109</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11000713</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/3583247</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muhondwa</surname><given-names>EP</given-names></name><collab>Semali</collab></person-group><article-title>Debriefing Note: Study preparation of a community-based PMTCT in Mtwara rural district. </article-title><year>2004</year><comment>(Unpublished Report)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jahn</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kowalewski</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimatta</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Obstetric care in southern Tanzania: does it reach those i